  (text "USB-C INPUT (5 V sink, USB 2.0 device, no Power Delivery)\n- R1/R2: 5.1k Rd on each CC pin separately (USB Type-C sink requirement).\n- USB_CC1/USB_CC2 go to MCU ADC inputs to read source current (0.5/1.5/3 A).\n- U2 clamps D+/D- and VBUS. Both pins of each I/O pair are one node: route through the part.\n- C1 kept small: a sink may present at most 10 uF on VBUS.\nTODO before review: 20 V-tolerant CC protection (TPD4S311-class, no library symbol yet);\nVBUS over-voltage is handled by the charger input rating - confirm from charger datasheet;\nshield-to-ground scheme (R3) to be decided with the enclosure ESD path."
    (at 20 20 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.8 1.8)
      )
      (justify left top)
    )
    (uuid faba7868-27a9-5ad2-a8a4-1f1dd3d14cf8)
  )
